  "content": {
    "id": "p67-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "The diastolic measurement for blood pressure in 35-year-old people is normally distributed with a mean of 75 and a standard deviation of 12.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p67-q2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "A person is considered to have low blood pressure if their diastolic measurement is 63 or less. Using the 68% empirical-rule approximation, what percentage of 35-year-olds have low blood pressure?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Approximately $16\\%$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}z(63)&=\\frac{63-75}{12}\\\\z(63)&=-1\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the empirical rule and symmetry:\n$$\\begin{align*}P(X\\le63)&=P(Z\\le-1)\\\\P(X\\le63)&\\approx\\frac{100-68}{2}\\%\\\\P(X\\le63)&\\approx16\\%.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 19
      },
      {
        "id": "p67-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Calculate the $z$-score for a diastolic measurement of 57.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-1.5$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}z(57)&=\\frac{57-75}{12}\\\\z(57)&=-1.5\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 14
      },
      {
        "id": "p67-q2-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "The probability that a 35-year-old person has a diastolic measurement between 57 and 63 can be found by evaluating $\\displaystyle\\int_a^b f(x)\\,dx$, where $a$ and $b$ are constants and $f(x)=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{2\\pi}}e^{-x^2/2}$ is the standard normal PDF. By first finding $a$ and $b$, calculate an approximate value for this probability using the trapezoidal rule with 3 function values. Give the probability to 4 decimal places.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=-1.5$, $b=-1$; probability $\\approx0.0921$ (approximately $9.2\\%$).",
          "worked": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p67-q2-c-conversion",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
